      },
    },
    {
      role: "problem", time: 60,
      notes: `Here is the problem. The idea that spread was the 30-minute "anabolic window": miss the shake right after the lift and the work is wasted.

The research is calmer than that. When a meta-analysis pulled the protein-timing trials together and controlled for how much protein people ate overall, timing on its own added little. Total daily protein was the strongest predictor of muscle gain. The ISSN position stand now says the same thing: hit the daily total, spread across the day.

