Where timing really earns its keep is when sessions are long, or close together. Two sessions less than eight hours apart, a doubleheader, a tournament day: then what you eat right after the first one decides how you start the second. Outside those cases, a well-fed day does most of the work.`,
      build(s) {
        s.headline("Timing matters most when sessions run long or close together.", { y: 1.2, w: 10.5, h: 1.25, size: 40 });
